      "fieldData": {
       "meta-title": "Post Webinar Survey Builder and Question Guide | Emergent",
       "meta-description": "Create a post webinar survey with the right questions, open it from any webinar tool, and send demo requests to your CRM. Free to start.",
       "name": "Build a Post Webinar Survey That Shapes Your Next Session",
       "acrm---product-name": "Post Webinar Survey Builder",
       "description": "Build a post webinar survey attendees open as the session ends, with demo requests sent to your CRM and every answer saved.",
       "acrm---breadcrumb": "Post Webinar Survey",
       "explore-cta": "Build My Post Webinar Survey",
       "awb---how-to-title": "How to Create a Post Webinar Survey",
       "awb---how-to-description": "Seven steps to plan a post webinar survey, build it with Emergent, and act on what attendees tell you.",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Webinar Survey FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are some good questions to include in a post-webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Open on how attendees rate the session overall, from 1 to 5, and what they found most useful. Then ask what was still unclear, how each speaker did, and which topic they want covered next. Finish on the step the webinar was meant to drive, such as a demo request. Write each of these post-webinar survey questions about the session you ran, not about webinars in general.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a post webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe the webinar, its audience, and the questions you want in a plain-English prompt, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns it into a working survey with a results dashboard and a database behind it. Publish it, put the link on your closing slide and in the replay email, and edit any question later with one more prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a post-webinar survey template enough, or should each session get its own?\", \"a\": \"A post-webinar survey template is a fine start for the rating and comment questions, which stay the same every time. Write the rest for the session: name the topic in the usefulness question and match the closing question to the webinar's goal. With Emergent, you describe those changes in a prompt and the survey is rebuilt to match.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a post-webinar survey different from one for an in-person event?\", \"a\": \"It asks about the stream itself: whether the audio and video played without breaking up, and whether attendees stayed to the end. It leaves out the venue and catering questions that a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/post-event'>post event survey</a> covers.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best time to show a post-webinar survey to attendees?\", \"a\": \"Show it the moment the session ends, then send it again with the replay. A Zoom webinar host can schedule a survey to be sent to attendees and panelists when the webinar ends, and can redirect them to a third-party survey service instead. Close the survey after about a week, while attendees still remember the session.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a post-webinar survey have?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to 8 questions or fewer for an hour-long webinar, and about 5 for a 30-minute one. Put the rating first and the demo question last, since those two feed the next decision. Anything past that limit can go in a follow-up survey to the people who asked to hear more.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I run a post-webinar survey after an online class or a livestreamed service?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The core questions carry over: rate the session and say what was still unclear. For a livestreamed service, ask about the stream itself, such as sound and video, and leave questions about congregation life to a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/church'>church survey</a>. Emergent builds either one from a prompt, with no response cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a post-webinar survey be anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Keep the ratings anonymous and the contact details optional. People rate a session more freely when their name is not attached, but a demo request is useless without a name and email. Ask for contact details only in the question where someone asks for a next step, and say so in that question.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get more attendees to answer a post-webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Ask while they are still in the session. Mention the survey before the last audience question, show the link as a QR code on the last slide, and make the first question a single tap. Send one reminder with the replay link and stop there. Each response is saved to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a post-webinar survey sign people up for a next step like volunteering?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add a yes-or-no question for the next step and have the app add each yes to a sign-up list with the person's name and email. To collect availability and preferred shifts, send a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/volunteer'>volunteer survey</a> to the people who said yes instead of lengthening the webinar survey.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a post webinar survey that collects every answer in a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a post webinar survey that collects every answer in a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Demo Requests\", \"add\": \"Add demo requests that send each attendee who asks for a demo to HubSpot.\"}, {\"label\": \"Session Ratings\", \"add\": \"Add session ratings on a 1-5 scale and average them on the dashboard.\"}, {\"label\": \"Phone Layout\", \"add\": \"Add a phone layout that shows one question per screen.\"}, {\"label\": \"Speaker Feedback\", \"add\": \"Add speaker feedback questions that rate each presenter.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
       "thumbnail-image": {
        "fileId": "6ad220c3304f2eea525454e5",
        "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6a0f028de6df6a6fd88c3f89/6ad220c3304f2eea525454e5_og.webp",
        "alt": "Build a post webinar survey with Emergent"
       }
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf3f2ad9386565b4a8fd49",
      "fieldData": {
       "meta-title": "Post Event Survey Questions and Builder | Emergent",
       "meta-description": "Build a post event survey from a prompt that asks about the sessions each person attended and sends low scores to the owner who can act.",
       "name": "Build a Post Event Survey Tied to Who Attended What",
       "acrm---product-name": "Post Event Survey Builder",
       "description": "Build a post event survey that knows who attended what, saves every answer to a database you own, and flags low scores.",
       "acrm---breadcrumb": "Post Event Survey",
       "explore-cta": "Build My Post Event Survey",
       "acrm---why-emergent-title": "Why Build Your Post Event Survey With Emergent?",
       "awb---integration-feature-2": "<h3>What registrants came for, and whether they got it</h3><p>A week before a Saturday workshop, each registrant picks the topic they most want covered. The post event survey then names that pick and asks whether today covered it. Both answers sit on one registrant row. Of the 14 people who came for pricing, 5 said yes. Pricing moves to the top of the next agenda.</p>",
       "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { conference: \"Build a post event survey for my two-day conference. The morning after it closes, email each attendee a list of only the sessions their badge was scanned into, and ask them to rate each one out of 5 with an optional comment. Average the scores by session and track. When a session averages below 3.5, email the program chair the score and every comment.\", expoExhibitors: \"Build an exhibitor survey for my home show. Two days after it ends, email every exhibitor questions on booth traffic and lead quality, then ask whether they will book again: yes, no, or not sure. Save the answers to each exhibitor's record with their booth number. For any no or not sure, create a follow-up for my sales manager with the booth and the comment.\", beforeAndAfter: \"Build a pre and post survey for my Saturday workshop. A week before, ask each registrant to pick the topic they most want covered from a list of four. After the workshop, ask them by name whether today covered that topic. Keep both answers on the same registrant row. Show me a count per topic: who came for it and who said yes.\", musicFestival: \"Build a nightly survey for my three-day music festival. Each evening, email ticket holders a question on how long entry took, scored out of 5. Save each answer with the gate from their ticket scan. By morning, show the average entry score for each gate and flag the lowest one for my operations lead.\" };</p>",
       "awb---how-to-title": "How to Run a Post Event Survey",
       "awb---how-to-description": "Seven steps to plan a post event survey whose answers change what you do at the next event.",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Event Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are good post-event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good post event survey questions are short, specific, and about something the person experienced, like a session they sat in or the line at check-in. Use one rating scale throughout so scores compare across sessions. Leave out anything the person could not judge, such as the event budget or the choice of caterer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a post event survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe the event, who attended, and what you want to learn in a prompt. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> drafts the questions, the send time, and the table that stores every answer. Publish it, then share the link by email or on a QR code printed on signs at the exits.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an event feedback form include?\", \"a\": \"An event feedback form needs a few fields besides the questions: the person's role (attendee, speaker, or exhibitor), the sessions they attended, and a checkbox asking whether you may follow up. Those fields let you split answers by group and reply to complaints. Keep the form short enough to finish on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an event feedback survey be anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Make it anonymous when the questions judge people, and named when you need to follow up. A named event feedback survey lets you call back an unhappy exhibitor or tie each answer to the sessions someone attended. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/church'>church survey</a> that asks about a pastor is a good case for anonymity; feedback on a parish picnic can carry names.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good pre event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good pre event survey questions ask what people want from the event while you can still plan for it. Ask which topic they most want covered, any dietary or access needs, and which sessions they plan to attend. Their answers set room sizes and catering counts, and give the post event survey something to check against.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you send after event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Send attendees after event survey questions within a day of the close, while people still remember which sessions they sat through. For a multi-day event, a short survey each evening catches problems you can still fix the next morning. Send one reminder to anyone who has not answered after three days.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some examples of post event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Five that fit a conference or a trade show: How would you rate the event overall? Which session will you use at work? Was anything hard to find, such as rooms or food? Would you come next year? What one change would you make? For a paid event, add the value question a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-feedback'>customer feedback survey</a> would ask: was the ticket worth the price?\"}, {\"q\": \"Should post event survey questions for attendees differ from those for speakers?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Attendees judge content, logistics, and value for the ticket, while speakers judge the room, the audio setup, and the audience they got. Send each group its own short version, and tag every answer with the group so you can read them apart. Emergent builds every version in one app, with no cap on how many responses come in.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an event feedback survey template you can start from?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Describe your event in a prompt, such as a two-day conference with 30 sessions and 40 exhibitors, and Emergent drafts a starting template: questions, rating scales, and the table behind them. Rename a session, add a question, or split the survey by audience with a follow-up prompt instead of editing each field.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an event satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"An event satisfaction survey measures how satisfied people were with one event, through an overall score and a rating for each part. It is shorter than a full post event survey, and repeating it after every event lets you compare scores over time. For a company offsite, keep it apart from an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-satisfaction'>employee satisfaction survey</a>, which asks about the job, not the day.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a post event survey that collects every answer in a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a post event survey that collects every answer in a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Event Questions\", \"add\": \"Add eight event questions that mix ratings with open answers.\"}, {\"label\": \"Session Ratings\", \"add\": \"Add a rating out of 5 for each session the attendee checked into.\"}, {\"label\": \"Exhibitor Survey\", \"add\": \"Add an exhibitor survey that asks if each booth will book again.\"}, {\"label\": \"Pre-Event Survey\", \"add\": \"Add a pre-event survey that asks what each registrant came to learn.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
       "awb---key-feature-1-image": {
        "fileId": "6acf3f22d9386565b4a8fd04",
        "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6a0f028de6df6a6fd88c3f89/6acf3f22d9386565b4a8fd04_uc-1.svg",
        "alt": "A post event survey shows the freight forecasting panel at 3.2 out of 5 from 41 ratings, below the 3.5 line, and emails the program chair every comment."
